#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ndlink-watch -- the phone in a window: panel, speaker and keypad.

    ndlink-watch --host H [--port 5901] [--view-only] [--no-audio]
                 [--no-mute] [--latency MS] [--scale N] [--verbose]

Run by `ndlink watch`. Speaks nd-watchd's protocol (neodct/src/watchd/
nd-watchd.c has the wire format at the top; this file does not repeat it).

============ WHY NOT A VNC CLIENT ANY MORE ============

watch used to exec whatever VNC client it found. RFB has no audio, stock
clients scale badly or not at all, and nd-vncd was pinned to 10 fps for a link
that negotiated 10 Mbit/s. On the 100 Mbit link a whole-screen change at 30 fps
is a fifth of the wire. nd-vncd is still on the phone for any other client;
`ndlink watch --vnc` still opens one.

============ SCALING ============

The window is resizable and the panel is fitted to it with the aspect kept.
"sharp" (the default) scales by the largest whole factor with nearest-neighbour
and then smooths only the remaining fraction, so a 1-pixel line stays one even
width across the screen -- plain nearest at 3.4x makes every fifth column
fatter, which on a bitmap font reads as a rendering bug. F2 cycles sharp,
nearest and smooth.

============ AUDIO ============

What the phone plays arrives in the card's format (S16_LE stereo, 44.1 or
48 kHz on the C-Media) and is piped to the desktop's own player -- pw-play,
else paplay, else aplay -- so it follows whatever output the desktop is set
to. AudioOut says why that is not SDL. Anything the player cannot take within
about --latency ms is dropped, whole frames at a time, so a stall on the wire
costs a skip rather than a delay that never goes away.

The phone's own speaker is switched off while the window is open (and back
on when it closes) so the sound is not heard twice; --no-mute leaves it on,
F4 toggles it. nd-watchd.c has how, and why it cannot leave a phone silent.

--verbose opens a second window showing every key the phone is taking in --
its own keypad included -- with its CPU and RAM every ten seconds.

Keys: arrows, Enter = NaviKey, Backspace/Esc = C, 0-9, * #, M = menu.
F2 scaling, F3 mute here, F4 mute the phone, F11 fullscreen, Ctrl+Q quits.
"""

